==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[tottered]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|tatered|lang=enm}}, {{term|tatird|lang=en}}, from {{etyl|non|en}}. Originally, it was derived from the noun, but it was later it reanalysed as a past participle, ({{suffix|tatter|ed|lang=en}}), whereafter the verb came into being. Compare {{term|tatter|lang=en}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# rent in [[tatter]]s, [[torn]], hanging in [[rag]]s; [[ragged]]
#* '''1919''', [[w:Boris Sidis|Boris Sidis]], ''[[s:The Source and Aim of Human Progress|The Source and Aim of Human Progress]]'':
#*: ''The chattering, irrational brute of the subconscious clothes itself in the '''tattered''' garments of rationality and idealism.''
# [[dress]]ed in [[tatter]]s or [[rag]]s; [[ragged]]
